<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Society for the Revival of Kurdistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Komeley Jiyanewey Kurdistan, Komala JK</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Society for the Revival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurdistan">Kurdistan</a>, known as Komala, was a secret Kurdish nationalist organisation founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabad">Mahabad</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in 1942, during the Allied occupation of the country. It promoted Kurdish autonomy, language and culture. In 1945 it was transformed into the Kurdistan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-uganda">Democratic Party</a> of Iran under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qazi-muhammad">Qazi Muhammad</a>, which proclaimed the Republic of Mahabad in January 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/society-for-the-revival-of-kurdistan.jpg" alt="Society for the Revival of Kurdistan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: محک, Zt-freak, Thespoondragon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_Mahabad.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
